The task of topical blog post retrieval is a complex task.
The relevance of a blog post is determined by the  topic .
We use textual credibility indicators to improve the retrieval process.
We consider two groups of indicators : post level and blog level.
We estimate these indicators and integrate them into a retrieval approach based on language models.
Experiments on the TREC Blog track test set show that both groups of credibility indicators significantly improve retrieval effectiveness.
The best performance is achieved when combining them.

